questions.modelAnswer:
A good tool includes:
* the two special triangles with side lengths;
* the unit circle with all multiples of $\frac{\pi}{6}$ and $\frac{\pi}{4}$ marked and their coordinates;
* a CAST diagram and the reference-angle rules (QII $\pi-\theta$, QIII $\theta-\pi$, QIV $2\pi-\theta$);
* a procedure: find quadrant → reference angle → special-triangle value → sign.

Example uses: $\cos\frac{7\pi}{6}$: QIII, ref $\frac{\pi}{6}$, cos negative → $-\frac{\sqrt3}{2}$. $\tan\frac{7\pi}{4}$: QIV, ref $\frac{\pi}{4}$, tan negative → $-1$.
